<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Issue gus-live-agentforce-provider-auth. RECONCILED against a live
  `sf project retrieve` of the real GTM_Agentforce_API Named Credential
  created in gtm-staging Setup (2026-09-25) — this is the actual metadata
  shape (note it differs from the first draft: allowMergeFieldsInBody/
  allowMergeFieldsInHeader/generateAuthorizationHeader/calloutStatus are
  top-level elements, not namedCredentialParameters entries, and the
  ExternalCredential link uses a nested <externalCredential> child rather
  than a parameterValue). See docs/architecture/gus-chat-provider-settings.md
  §5a for the full reconciliation record.

  RE-RECONCILED against a second live retrieve (2026-09-25) after the
  coordinator changed the Url live from the org's My Domain base to
  `https://api.salesforce.com`. This matches current Salesforce docs
  (developer.salesforce.com/docs/ai/agentforce/guide/agent-api-get-started.html
  and .../agent-api-considerations.html, fetched live 2026-09-25): the
  Agent API's base host IS `api.salesforce.com` (or `api.gov.salesforce.com`
  on Government Cloud), NOT the org's My Domain — the My Domain URL is
  instead required INSIDE the Start Session POST body, as
  `instanceConfig.endpoint`. So the earlier "STILL OPEN" note in the prior
  version of this file about my-domain-vs-api.salesforce.com is now
  resolved: `api.salesforce.com` is correct per the docs, confirmed as the
  live-configured value.

  RESOLVED (2026-09-25, later same day): the earlier "STILL OPEN" 404
  noted here was NOT the OAuth-scope gap suspected at the time (that was
  investigated and ruled out with evidence). The real cause was two
  things together: (1) the External Client App had "Issue JSON Web Token
  (JWT)-based access tokens for named users" unchecked, so client-credentials
  flow minted an opaque token this gateway can't route on; (2) the Start
  Session POST body's `instanceConfig.endpoint` needs a TRAILING SLASH
  (e.g. `https://your-domain.my.salesforce.com/`) to match Salesforce's
  own documented example exactly — omitting it 404s even with a valid JWT.
  Live proof (HTTP 200, real sessionId, real agent welcome message) is in
  §5a's "RESOLVED" subsection in docs/architecture/gus-chat-provider-settings.md.
  Any Apex that calls this Named Credential's session endpoint MUST include
  the trailing slash in instanceConfig.endpoint.
-->
<NamedCredential xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <allowMergeFieldsInBody>false</allowMergeFieldsInBody>
    <allowMergeFieldsInHeader>false</allowMergeFieldsInHeader>
    <calloutStatus>Enabled</calloutStatus>
    <generateAuthorizationHeader>true</generateAuthorizationHeader>
    <label>GTM Agentforce API</label>
    <namedCredentialParameters>
        <parameterName>Url</parameterName>
        <parameterType>Url</parameterType>
        <parameterValue>https://api.salesforce.com</parameterValue>
    </namedCredentialParameters>
    <namedCredentialParameters>
        <externalCredential>GTM_Agentforce_Credential</externalCredential>
        <parameterName>ExternalCredential</parameterName>
        <parameterType>Authentication</parameterType>
    </namedCredentialParameters>
    <namedCredentialType>SecuredEndpoint</namedCredentialType>
</NamedCredential>
